[center][size=6][b]KNOX ATLAS[/b][/size][/center]
[center][size=4][i]A read-only Project Zomboid interactive map and companion atlas.[/i][/size][/center]
[center][url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Knox-Atlas/releases][b]DOWNLOAD LATEST RELEASE[/b][/url]  |  [url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Knox-Atlas][b]VIEW SOURCE ON GITHUB[/b][/url][/center]

Knox Atlas is a standalone Windows Project Zomboid interactive map and companion application. It reads the game data installed on your computer and displays towns, streets, businesses, building types, likely resources, possible vehicle zones, and useful world coordinates.

[b]Knox Atlas is read-only.[/b] It does not install into Project Zomboid, modify the game, or write into your saves. It reads the local Steam installation and limited save metadata, then stores personal markers and preferences in its own application storage.

[center][url=https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228406-1345422498.png][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228406-1345422498.png[/img][/url][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]✨ Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]🗺️ [b]Game-derived map[/b] — water, terrain, roads, railways, buildings, towns, landmarks, and street names are read from the files installed with the game.
[*]🔎 [b]Search and coordinate travel[/b] — find places by name or jump directly to an X/Y coordinate.
[*]🏪 [b]Expandable filters[/b] — focus on individual business, building, likely-loot, resource, and vehicle categories.
[*]🎒 [b]Likely-loot hints[/b] — useful zones are labeled as likely locations, not guaranteed live inventory.
[*]🚙 [b]Drivable vehicle pools[/b] — inspect possible car, van, truck, utility, and emergency vehicle spawn areas.
[*]📍 [b]Named custom markers[/b] — save up to 100 colored points locally and keep them visible across the map.
[*]📏 [b]Distance measurement[/b] — drop multiple points, see their combined direct tile distance, and save named colored paths locally.
[*]📂 [b]Selectable local source[/b] — automatically discover Steam libraries or choose another ProjectZomboid installation folder from the app.
[*]🧭 [b]Map helpers[/b] — copy stable clicked coordinates and save a favorite center/zoom view.
[*]🖥️ [b]Second-monitor use[/b] — keep the atlas open beside the game or check it while playing.
[/list]

[line]

[size=5][b]🗺️ Explore and filter[/b][/size]

Pan and zoom around the game-derived map, search for a town, street, or business, or jump directly to an X/Y coordinate. The left-hand controls let you show only the information you need. Expand a category to choose its individual filters—for example, showing gas stations and medical locations while hiding the other business types.

[center][url=https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228474-1392741985.png][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228474-1392741985.png[/img][/url][/center]

[size=5][b]📍 Save your places and paths[/b][/size]

Click a location to view and copy its stable coordinates or save it as a named, color-coded marker. Choose [b]Measure distance[/b] to place multiple waypoints, see their combined direct tile distance, and save the finished measurement as a named path. Markers and paths remain visible across the map and are stored locally by Knox Atlas.

[center][url=https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228428-487330647.png][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228428-487330647.png[/img][/url][/center]

[line]

[size=5][b]⬇️ Installation[/b][/size]

Knox Atlas is a standalone companion, not an in-game mod. Do not place it in the Project Zomboid Mods folder.

[b][color=#d99b55]Choose one download—you do not need both.[/color][/b]

[size=4][b]Choosing the game installation[/b][/size]

Knox Atlas first checks the standard Steam installation and Steam's configured library folders. The usual Windows location is [font=Courier New]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\ProjectZomboid[/font].

If the game is elsewhere, click [b]Local game source[/b] in the lower-left corner of Knox Atlas. Choose the [font=Courier New]ProjectZomboid[/font] folder itself and click [b]Select Folder[/b]. The correct folder contains [font=Courier New]projectzomboid.jar[/font] and the [font=Courier New]media[/font] directory. Knox Atlas validates and remembers the selection without modifying the game files.

[center][url=https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228491-2097596346.png][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/583/images/368/368-1786228491-2097596346.png[/img][/url][/center]

[size=4][b]Windows Installer (recommended)[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download [b]Knox-Atlas-0.1.1-Windows-x64-setup.exe[/b].
[*]Double-click the downloaded file and follow the Windows setup prompts.
[*]Launch [b]Knox Atlas[/b] from the shortcut created by the installer.
[*]To remove it later, use [b]Settings → Apps → Installed apps[/b] in Windows.
[/list]

The installer creates Windows shortcuts and a standard uninstall entry.

[size=4][b]Portable ZIP (optional)[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Download [b]Knox-Atlas-0.1.1-Windows-x64-portable.zip[/b].
[*]Right-click the ZIP and choose [b]Extract All[/b]. Do not run Knox Atlas from inside the ZIP preview.
[*]Move the extracted folder somewhere writable where you intend to keep it.
[*]Run [b]Knox-Atlas.exe[/b] from that folder and keep the included files together.
[*]To remove the portable copy later, close Knox Atlas and delete the extracted folder.
[/list]

The portable package does not add shortcuts or a Windows uninstall entry and expects the Microsoft WebView2 runtime to already be installed. Download WebView2 only from Microsoft's [url=https://developer.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-edge/webview2/]official WebView2 Runtime page[/url]. Knox Atlas searches configured Steam libraries automatically; if needed, click the Local game source card and choose the ProjectZomboid installation folder.

Markers, saved paths, the preferred map view, and the selected game folder are stored automatically for the current Windows account under [font=Courier New]%LOCALAPPDATA%\com.pzcompanion.map[/font]. They are not kept inside the portable folder, so replacing or moving that folder does not normally erase them. Another computer or Windows account has separate storage. See the [url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Knox-Atlas/blob/main/docs/portable.md]portable guide on GitHub[/url] for WebView2 check commands and best-effort backup instructions.

[size=4][b]Using the portable build with Vortex[/b][/size]

Knox Atlas is added to Vortex as a tool, not installed as a Project Zomboid mod:
[list=1]
[*]Use [b]Manual Download[/b] on Nexus, then extract the portable ZIP normally.
[*]In Vortex, open [b]Dashboard[/b] and choose [b]Add Tool[/b].
[*]Set [b]Target[/b] to the extracted [font=Courier New]Knox-Atlas.exe[/font].
[*]Confirm [b]Start In[/b] is the folder containing the EXE, name it [b]Knox Atlas[/b], and save.
[/list]

Do not deploy the portable ZIP into the Project Zomboid game or Mods folder. The [url=https://github.com/TheMysticTurtle/Knox-Atlas/blob/main/docs/vortex.md]Vortex guide on GitHub[/url] records the complete compatibility notes.

[b][color=#d99b55]🛡️ Antivirus / SmartScreen:[/color][/b] Knox Atlas is not currently code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen or antivirus software may warn about an unfamiliar or unsigned application. This is common for small independent projects, but please download files only from this Nexus page or the official GitHub Releases page. The complete source and release workflow are public on GitHub; you are warmly invited to inspect them or build the application yourself. If a warning looks unusual or you are uncertain about a file, do not run it until you are comfortable with its source.

[line]

[size=5][b]🗺️ What the layers mean[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Basemap, streets, buildings, and official labels[/b] come directly from the installed game files.
[*][b]Businesses and likely loot[/b] are broad hints inferred from game-authored zones. Actual items are not guaranteed.
[*][b]Vehicle pools[/b] are places where drivable vehicles may spawn, not confirmed live vehicles.
[*][b]Latest save location[/b] is the last saved in-game map view, not the player's live position.
[*][b]Custom markers[/b] are created by you and stored locally by Knox Atlas, never in the Project Zomboid save.
[*][b]Saved paths[/b] are measurements drawn by you and stored locally by Knox Atlas; they are not road-routing instructions.
[/list]

Random generation, sandbox settings, mods, player activity, and the current save determine what is actually present in the world.

[line]

[size=5][b]📌 Current scope — v0.1.1[/b][/size]

The current release targets Windows and the base English map. It does not currently track live players, read live container inventories, locate vehicle keys, identify randomized survivor houses, render building interiors/floors, or automatically merge enabled map mods.

The current scope reflects the data sources available to the application.

[line]

